# Implementation Plan - Phase 9: Offline Download & Storage System

This plan details the implementation of the secure offline-first course download and storage infrastructure for the Leitner Learning Platform mobile application.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Encryption Key Derivation**
> In accordance with the security design, we will derive the local SQLite decryption key using **PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256** with 10,000 iterations from a client-side device-unique identifier and a user salt. 
> Since the backend database currently does not store or return an independent user-specific cryptographic salt, we will generate a cryptographically secure 32-byte user salt locally upon the user's first successful authentication/profile completion. This salt will be persisted in `FlutterSecureStorage` (iOS Keychain / Android Keystore) and used to derive the database encryption key. This keeps the encryption key fully secure and isolated locally.

> [!WARNING]
> **Dynamic RAM Decryption of Media**
> Pre-encrypted course media assets (images, audio) inside the downloaded ZIP file must be decrypted in-memory (RAM) during card study to prevent unencrypted premium content from being written to device disk. We will incorporate the `encrypt` Dart package to handle AES-256-CBC decryption of files in-memory before visual/audio playback.

